  "chitchat": [
    "Corva polishes a glass that was already clean, watching the room in the mirror.",
    "\"Printer does the pretty ones. I do the ones that work.\""
  ],
  "description": "A lean, watchful woman working the rail with the economy of someone who's poured for every ego the station ever put a byline on. She lets the drink-printer do the theatre and keeps the real bottles behind her, one hand always near the one that matters. Nothing you say will surprise her, and she'll let you believe otherwise.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "\"Tab's open. So's the door.\" She's already reading the next face in the mirror."
    },
    "gossip": {
      "actions": [
        {
          "action": "GOSSIP_TELL"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Back.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Corva keeps polishing. The glass doesn't move, and neither does her voice. \"Everyone talks at a rail. It's the mirror — they forget I'm reading it too.\""
    },
    "guest": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Get me those drinks.",
          "next": "__shop__"
        },
        {
          "label": "Back.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Back booth, under the warm lamp, rewriting the same cold open for the fourth time.\" She tips her head toward the curtain. \"Buy him a drink if you're feeling charitable. Buy yourself two if you're going to ask him what it's about.\""
    },
    "menu": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Set me up.",
          "next": "__shop__"
        },
        {
          "label": "Back.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"The printer'll sell you a House Fizz that glows and lies about what's in it — that's most people's night, right there. Or I pour you a rust whiskey and we both keep our dignity.\" A flicker of a smile. \"Beer if you're pacing yourself, which, in here, nobody is.\""
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "What's good?",
          "next": "menu"
        },
        {
          "label": "Pour me something.",
          "next": "__shop__"
        },
        {
          "label": "Who's in the back booth?",
          "next": "guest"
        },
        {
          "label": "Nothing for now.",
          "next": "bye"
        },
        {
          "label": "Quiet night. Anything moving out there?",
          "next": "gossip"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Press or crew?\" Corva doesn't look up from the glass she's polishing. \"Doesn't matter. Everyone drinks the same in here — like the page is still open and the deadline's still moving.\" She sets the glass down. \"What'll it be?\""
    }
  },
